.TH TDE\-MIXER 1 "November 2026" "tde-mixer 0.1.0" "Trinity Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
tde\-mixer \- per\-application volume mixer for PipeWire and PulseAudio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tde\-mixer
.RB [ \-\-page
.IR page ]
.RB [ \-\-backend
.IR backend ]
.RI [ "generic TDE and TQt options" ]
.br
.B tde\-mixer
.RB [ \-\-backend
.IR backend ]
.B \-\-list
|
.BI \-\-volume " percent"
|
.B \-\-toggle\-mute
.br
.B tdecmshell mixer
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tde\-mixer
is a volume mixer for the Trinity Desktop Environment. It controls the
sound server,
.BR pipewire (1)
or
.BR pulseaudio (1),
rather than the channels of a sound card like
.BR kmix (1).
.PP
It shows one volume slider, mute button and level meter for each
application that plays or records sound, and lets you move an application
to another output or input device. It also sets the volume, port and
default status of each device, and the profile of each sound card.
.PP
The same mixer is available as a Trinity Control Center module, under
.B Sound & Multimedia \(-> Volume Mixer
or with
.BR "tdecmshell mixer" ,
which adds a Settings tab, and in System Settings under
.BR "Computer Administration" .
The system tray icon is
.BR tde\-mixer\-tray (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " page"
The page shown at start:
.BR playback " (default), " recording ", " output ", " input " or " configuration .
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " backend"
.B pipewire
talks to PipeWire directly;
.B pulse
uses the PulseAudio protocol, which works with PulseAudio and with
PipeWire's pulse server;
.B auto
uses PipeWire if it is running and PulseAudio otherwise. The default is
the backend chosen in the settings
.RB ( auto
unless changed).
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print the devices (the default marked with
.BR * ),
the applications playing and recording sound and the sound cards, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-volume " percent"
Set the volume of the default output device and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-toggle\-mute
Mute or unmute the default output device and exit.
.PP
The last three options need no X display. All generic TDE and TQt options,
such as
.BR \-\-help\-all ,
are also accepted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 if the sound server cannot be reached within five seconds,
3 if there is no output device.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.trinity/share/config/tde\-mixerrc
Settings, group
.BR [General] :
.B Backend
(auto, pipewire, pulse),
.B VolumeStep
(percent),
.BR AllowOverAmplify ,
.BR ShowPeaks ,
.BR ReplaceKMix .
.TP
.I ~/.trinity/share/config/tde\-mixer\-trayrc
Settings of the tray icon, see
.BR tde\-mixer\-tray (1).
.PP
Volumes, devices and profiles are not stored by tde\-mixer but by the
sound server (WirePlumber or PulseAudio's restore modules).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tde\-mixer\-tray (1),
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR wireplumber (1),
.BR wpctl (1),
.BR pulseaudio (1),
.BR pactl (1),
.BR kmix (1)
.PP
The handbook is available in the TDE Help Center
.RI ( help:/tde\-mixer ).
.SH BUGS
Please report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/Yjlion/tde-mixer/issues
.UE .
